.TH PARU-WRAPPER 1 "November 2026" "paru-wrapper 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
paru-wrapper \- Enhanced paru wrapper with local AUR repository management, modular plugin hooks, and VCS migrations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B paru-wrapper
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPARU_ARGS\fR...]
.br
.B paru-wrapper
\fB\-\-init\-repo\fR \fIREPO_NAME\fR \fIREPO_DIR\fR \fIPROJECTS_DIR\fR
.br
.B paru-wrapper
\fB\-\-connect\-repo\fR \fIREPO_NAME\fR \fIREPO_DIR\fR \fIPROJECTS_DIR\fR
.br
.B paru-wrapper
\fB\-\-wrapper\-help\fR
.br
.B paru-wrapper
\fB\-\-wrapper\-version\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B paru-wrapper
is a wrapper around the \fBparu\fR AUR helper and \fBpacman\fR package manager on Arch Linux.
It automates local custom repository management, performs dependency-aware orphan pruning (preserving toolchains and target \fImakedepends\fR by default), batches \fIFORCE_REBUILD\fR installations into a single \fBpacman \-U\fR transaction while guarding temporarily masked pacman hooks with a PID lockfile, retries transient AUR RPC failures, runs \fBghc-pkg check\fR preflight diagnostics for Haskell packages, falls back to non-\fB-git\fR release packages on broken \fB-git\fR builds (tracked in \fI~/.local/state/paru-wrapper/git-fallbacks.tsv\fR), provides modular plugin hooks, supports interactive search-and-install (deferring pre-transaction project updates and repository synchronization until packages are selected for installation), and supports migrating packages to bleeding-edge VCS \fB-git\fR variants via \fB\-\-gittinator\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-gittinator
Scans installed AUR packages and migrates them to development VCS (\-git) variants where available.
.TP
.B \-\-low\-priority
Runs \fBparu\fR and \fBmakepkg\fR builds with reduced CPU and I/O priority (enabled by default via \fIPARU_WRAPPER_LOW_PRIORITY\fR). Stripped before forwarding arguments to \fBparu\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-low\-priority
Disables low-priority CPU/I/O throttling for the current invocation. Stripped before forwarding arguments to \fBparu\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-batch
Installs each rebuilt \fIFORCE_REBUILD\fR AUR package individually instead of batching all built archives into a single \fBpacman \-U\fR call. Stripped before forwarding arguments to \fBparu\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-cleanup\-builddeps
Allows orphan cleanup to remove build-dependencies and toolchains (e.g. \fBrustup\fR, \fBcmake\fR, \fBmeson\fR, \fBghc\fR). Stripped before forwarding arguments to \fBparu\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cleanup\-builddeps
Preserves build-dependencies, toolchains, and target \fImakedepends\fR during orphan cleanup (default). Stripped before forwarding arguments to \fBparu\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-init\-repo \fIREPO_NAME\fR \fIREPO_DIR\fR \fIPROJECTS_DIR\fR
Initializes an empty custom local pacman repository database and writes the client configuration to \fI~/.config/paru-wrapper/paru-wrapper.conf\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-connect\-repo \fIREPO_NAME\fR \fIREPO_DIR\fR \fIPROJECTS_DIR\fR
Connects to an existing custom local pacman repository.
.TP
.B \-\-wrapper\-help
Displays the extended help message detailing wrapper-specific options, plugin hooks, and environment variables.
.TP
.B \-\-wrapper\-version
Displays the version of paru-wrapper.
.SH MODULAR PLUGINS
.B paru-wrapper
supports an event-driven plugin hook architecture. Plugins are shell scripts placed in:
.IP \(bu 2
\fI~/.config/paru-wrapper/plugins.d/\fR (user-specific overrides)
.IP \(bu 2
\fI/etc/paru-wrapper/plugins.d/\fR (system overrides)
.IP \(bu 2
\fI/usr/lib/paru-wrapper/plugins.d/\fR (packaged default plugins)
.PP
Plugins handle events: \fBpre-transaction\fR, \fBpost-transaction\fR, \fBpackage-rebuilt\fR, \fBdeferred-hooks\fR, and \fBpost-transaction-bg\fR.
.PP
Default plugins include:
.TP
.B 10-snapper.sh
Pre/post transaction Btrfs snapshots (requires \fBsnapper\fR).
.TP
.B 20-anneal.sh
Automatically unmarks packages from the rebuild queue upon recompilation (requires \fBanneal\fR).
.TP
.B 25-projects-pull.sh
Fetches fast-forward updates for clean git repositories residing in \fIPARU_WRAPPER_PROJECTS_DIR\fR and rebuilds/installs updated packages that are already installed.
.TP
.B 30-rebuild-check.sh
Analyzes installed packages for broken shared library bindings after system updates (requires \fBrebuild-check-hook\fR).
.TP
.B 40-paru-completion.sh
Regenerates shell tab completion cache files (requires \fBparu-completion-hook\fR).
.TP
.B 50-vault-sync.sh
Background configuration vault synchronization.
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B PARU_WRAPPER_AUTO_UPDATE_INSTALLED
When enabled (default), automatically upgrades local custom repository packages when a newer version is discovered in the AUR, and rebuilds/installs updated installed projects in \fIPARU_WRAPPER_PROJECTS_DIR\fR.
.TP
.B PARU_WRAPPER_LOW_PRIORITY
When enabled (default: \fItrue\fR), runs \fBparu\fR and \fBmakepkg\fR invocations under a low-priority \fBsystemd-run\fR user scope (\fICPUWeight=20\fR, \fIIOWeight=20\fR) with \fBnice -n 15\fR and \fBionice -c 3\fR, falling back to \fBnice\fR/\fBionice\fR when a user scope is unavailable.
.TP
.B PARU_WRAPPER_CLEANUP_BUILDDEPS
When set to \fI1\fR (or \fItrue\fR), orphan cleanup removes unused build-dependencies and toolchains; default \fI0\fR preserves toolchains and target \fImakedepends\fR.
.TP
.B PARU_WRAPPER_BATCH_INSTALL
When set to \fI1\fR (default), \fIFORCE_REBUILD\fR builds use \fBmakepkg \-Csf\fR and perform one batched \fBpacman \-U\fR install at the end of the build loop (with single-package fallback on failure).
.TP
.B PARU_WRAPPER_PKGSCAN_AUTO_ACCEPT_DANGER
Controls auto-acceptance of \fBverify_pkg\fR danger scores (default: \fI0\fR, allowing \fICLEAN\fR, \fISAFE_LOCAL_IDIOM\fR, and \fIACCEPT\fR verdicts while blocking \fISUSPICIOUS\fR and \fICRITICAL_RISK\fR). Set to \fI1\fR/\fItrue\fR to auto-accept non-critical warnings, or an integer threshold above 1.
.TP
.B PARU_WRAPPER_REPO
Custom local repository name.
.TP
.B PARU_WRAPPER_PROJECTS_DIR
Path to local development project checkouts (default: \fI~/Projects\fR).
.TP
.B PARU_WRAPPER_NET_RETRY_MAX
Maximum automatic resume retries after mid-download network interruptions or partial (\fI.part\fR) downloads (default: 5).
.TP
.B PARU_WRAPPER_NET_WAIT_TIMEOUT
Maximum seconds to wait for network connectivity recovery before aborting (default: 1800; 0 disables waiting).
.TP
.B PARU_WRAPPER_NET_CHECK_URL
URL probed to verify connectivity recovery (default: \fIhttps://archlinux.org\fR).
.TP
.B PARU_WRAPPER_BUILD_USER
Non-root user used for AUR/makepkg builds when \fBparu-wrapper\fR is invoked as root (defaults to \fISUDO_USER\fR or active session user).
.TP
.B PARU_WRAPPER_SRCDEST
Override \fBSRCDEST\fR directory used when validating and recovering stale \fBmakepkg\fR git source clones.
.TP
.B FORCE_REBUILD
When set to 1, forces recompilation of target packages from source.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR paru (8),
.BR pacman (8),
.BR makepkg (8)
